# The exceptional linear/unitary-three residual branch

The shared transfers identify the actual action quotients of conjugate
components, preserve their component images, reduce the inner three-residual
containment to the two-core and odd prime residuals, and supply the
tight-embedding and inversion arguments for the outer branch.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, the exceptional
case in the proof of 16.4.8, printed pp.1187–1188. The outer-action model
calculations, inner residual generation and U₃(8) exclusion are still needed
for final assembly. No completed source alternative is asserted here.
-/
